{% extends "@core/docs/_layout.twig" %}

{% block doc_content %}
<h1>Tutorial: Build a Complete Page</h1>
<p>
    Every other page in these docs explains one feature. This one puts them together. You will build the <strong>Recipe Box</strong>: a public gallery of community recipes with photos, pagination, a "save to favorites" button and a form for logged-in users to share their own recipe. By the end you will have used almost every part of the framework in a single, realistic feature, and seen where each piece belongs.
</p>

<p>The code follows the same rules as the framework itself: PHP 8.4, strict types, and everything is written to pass PHPStan level 9.</p>

<div class="bg-blue-100 border-l-4 border-blue-500 text-blue-700 p-4">
    <strong>How to use this page:</strong> follow the steps in order and you will end with a working feature. If you only need one technique, every step stands on its own and links to the full reference page for that feature.
</div>

<hr>

