<h2 id="session">Sessions at a Glance</h2>
<p>You used the session in four different ways without ever starting it: the front controller does that once per request.</p>

<div class="overflow-x-auto">
<table class="min-w-full text-left border border-gray-300 dark:border-gray-700">
<thead class="bg-gray-100 dark:bg-gray-800"><tr>
<th class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-gray-300 dark:border-gray-700">What</th>
<th class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-gray-300 dark:border-gray-700">How</th>
<th class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-gray-300 dark:border-gray-700">Where</th>
</tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">Who is logged in</td><td class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700"><code>Session::string('user_id')</code></td><td class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700"><code>store()</code>; the <code>auth</code> middleware checks the same key</td></tr>
<tr><td class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">One-time messages</td><td class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700"><code>redirect(...)-&gt;with('success', ...)</code>, shown by the layout</td><td class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700"><code>store()</code>, <code>favorite()</code></td></tr>
<tr><td class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">Favorites</td><td class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700"><code>Session::set('favorites', ...)</code> and <code>Session::get()</code></td><td class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700"><code>favorite()</code>, <code>show()</code></td></tr>
<tr><td class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">Recently viewed</td><td class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700"><code>Session::set('recent_recipes', ...)</code></td><td class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700"><code>rememberVisit()</code></td></tr>
<tr><td class="px-4 py-2">CSRF token</td><td class="px-4 py-2"><code>csrf_field()</code> and <code>csrf_token()</code></td><td class="px-4 py-2"><code>create.twig</code>, <code>show.twig</code></td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p>Favorites live in the session, so they belong to one browser and disappear when it closes. To keep them for good, store them in a table keyed by <code>user_id</code>: the controller code barely changes.</p>

