<th class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-gray-300 dark:border-gray-700">Likely cause and fix</th>
</tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700"><code>419 CSRF token mismatch</code></td><td class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">The form is missing <code>{% verbatim %}{{ csrf_field() }}{% endverbatim %}</code>, or the island is not sending <code>_token</code> in the JSON body.</td></tr>
<tr><td class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700"><code>/recipes/new</code> shows a recipe or a 404</td><td class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">The <code>{slug}</code> route is registered before the static one, or the route cache is stale. Reorder, then run <code>php rhapsody route:clear</code>.</td></tr>
<tr><td class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">Images return <code>403</code></td><td class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">The URL was not signed. Build it with <code>ImageSigner::url()</code>, as in <code>imageSet()</code>.</td></tr>
<tr><td class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">Images return <code>404</code></td><td class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">The Glide path is relative to <code>public/images/</code>. The file must be at <code>public/images/recipes/...</code>.</td></tr>
<tr><td class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">The islands do not appear</td><td class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">Run <code>npm run dev</code> with <code>VITE_DEV_SERVER=true</code> (or <code>npm run build</code> with it set to <code>false</code>) and check the browser console.</td></tr>
<tr><td class="px-4 py-2">Queued mail never arrives</td><td class="px-4 py-2">Is a worker running? Did you run <code>queue:install --migrate</code>? Is <code>MAIL_HOST</code> set in <code>.env</code>? Failed jobs show up with <code>php rhapsody queue:failed</code>.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>

<hr>

<h2 id="production">Before You Go Live</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Set <code>APP_ENV=production</code> and a strong <code>APP_KEY</code>.</strong> The key also signs your image URLs and queued jobs.</li>
    <li><strong>Build the front end:</strong> <code>VITE_DEV_SERVER=false</code> and <code>npm run build</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Cache routes and templates:</strong> <code>php rhapsody route:cache</code> and <code>php rhapsody app:cache-warm</code>. Re-run <code>route:clear</code> then <code>route:cache</code> whenever you add a route.</li>
    <li><strong>Keep the queue worker alive</strong> with Supervisor, or from cron on shared hosting, and restart it after each deploy so it loads the new code.</li>
    <li><strong>Make the directories writable:</strong> <code>storage/</code> (cache, logs, exports) and <code>public/images/recipes/</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Run PHPStan at level 9</strong> before you ship.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Security notes worth repeating</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Uploaded files are checked by content, renamed randomly and never allowed to keep an executable extension. We store recipe photos under <code>public/images/</code> so the image resizer can reach them. If you would rather keep originals private, upload to the default <code>storage/uploads</code> instead and point the <code>source</code> setting in <code>ImageController</code> there (see <a href="{{ base_url }}/docs/image-processing">Image Processing</a>).</li>
    <li>Twig escapes everything by default. The only <code>|raw</code> in this tutorial is the pagination HTML, which the framework builds itself.</li>
    <li>Every query that includes visitor input uses bound parameters.</li>
</ul>

<hr>

<h2 id="next">Where to Go Next</h2>
<p>You now have a pattern you can copy for any feature. A few ways to extend the Recipe Box and practise:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Edit and delete</strong> a recipe, allowing only its author: compare <code>Session::string('user_id')</code> to <code>getAuthorId()</code> and throw <code>HttpException(403)</code> otherwise.</li>
    <li><strong>Move the sort and page size into the URL</strong> and let the <a href="{{ base_url }}/docs/pagination">AJAX pagination</a> helper swap the list without a page reload.</li>
    <li><strong>Add a rate limit</strong> to the share form with your own <a href="{{ base_url }}/docs/middleware">middleware</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Persist favorites</strong> in a table so they follow the user between devices.</li>
    <li><strong>Test it:</strong> start from the <a href="{{ base_url }}/docs/testing">Unit Testing</a> guide.</li>
</ul>

